.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions implement the differential-dataflow
.Ql server
crate: a long-running host for several dataflows
.Pq Dq plugins
that share arrangements by name.
One plugin publishes an indexed collection
.Pq a trace
under a name through
.Fn dtfl_trace_handler_set ,
and other plugins import that same trace with
.Fn dtfl_trace_handler_get
and
.Xr dtfl_trace_import 3 ,
so the cost of indexing the collection is paid once and shared across every
importer.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_dd_server_new
creates a server with the host clock at epoch 0, writing status and output
to
.Fa out
.Pq or standard output when Dv NULL .
.Fn dtfl_dd_server_free
releases it.
.Fn dtfl_dd_server_epoch
returns the current open epoch.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_dd_server_register
registers a plugin so
.Fn dtfl_dd_server_load
can select it by name.
A
.Vt dtfl_dataflow_plugin
is a name and a build callback
.Pq Vt dtfl_dd_build_fn ,
the static-registration stand-in for a dynamically loaded shared object.
.Fn dtfl_dd_server_load
builds a new dataflow on the shared worker under
.Fa instance ,
passing the build callback the positional
.Fa argv
arguments.
It returns 0, or a
.Dv DTFL_E Ns Em *
code with a message through
.Xr dtfl_last_error_detail 3 .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_dd_server_tick
closes the current epoch, advances every plugin input, and runs the worker
to quiescence.
.Fn dtfl_dd_server_drop
drops a loaded instance, releasing its dataflow and the inputs it created.
.Fn dtfl_dd_server_peek
prints a registered trace's consolidated contents as of the current epoch.
.Fn dtfl_dd_server_list
prints the registry.
.Pp
The build callback receives a
.Vt dtfl_dd_env
describing its environment.
.Fn dtfl_dd_env_scope
is the dataflow scope to build in;
.Fn dtfl_dd_env_handles
is the shared trace handler;
.Fn dtfl_dd_env_probe
is the common probe to attach outputs to;
.Fn dtfl_dd_env_elapsed_ns
is nanoseconds since the server started;
.Fn dtfl_dd_env_argc
and
.Fn dtfl_dd_env_arg
are the load's positional arguments.
A plugin that creates its own input hands it to the server through
.Fn dtfl_dd_env_add_input ,
which advances and flushes it each
.Ic tick .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_dd_server_handles
returns the shared handler, so a caller can confirm that a trace is shared.
.Fn dtfl_trace_handler_has
reports whether a trace is registered under a name.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_dd_server_new
returns the server, or
.Dv NULL
only through the panic hook.
.Fn dtfl_dd_server_load ,
.Fn dtfl_dd_server_drop
and
.Fn dtfl_dd_server_peek
return 0 on success or a
.Dv DTFL_E Ns Em *
code.
.Fn dtfl_trace_handler_get
returns the handle, or
.Dv NULL
if no trace is registered under
.Fa name .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl-server 1 ,
.Xr dtfl_collection_arrange_by_key 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_trace_import 3
.Sh STANDARDS
Ported from the differential-dataflow
.Ql server
crate at tag
.Ql differential-dataflow-v0.25.1
.Pq Pa server/src/lib.rs , Pa server/src/bin/dd_server.rs .
Upstream loads plugins through
.Xr dlopen 3 ;
this port registers them statically, since library code may not
.Xr dlopen 3 .
